---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How Gemma 4's Multi-Token Prediction Works | AI/ML Deep Dives"
  description="A deep dive into Gemma4 Assistant: KV sharing, centroid-based vocab prediction, and bidirectional attention — with animated, annotated visualizations."
  crumb="How Gemma 4's MTP Works"
>

<style is:global>
/* ── Post variables ─────────────────────────────────────── */
.post-hero{padding:6.5rem 2rem 3rem;max-width:1700px;margin:0 auto}
.post-hero .tags{margin-bottom:1.25rem}
.post-hero h1{font-size:clamp(1.75rem,4.5vw,2.75rem);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.03em;line-height:1.1;margin-bottom:1.1rem;background:linear-gradient(150deg,var(--text) 35%,var(--muted2));-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;background-clip:text}
.post-hero .lead{font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--muted2);max-width:820px;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.75rem}
.post-hero-meta{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.25rem;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);padding-top:1.25rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}

/* ── Two-column layout ─────────────────────────────────── */
.post-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 560px;align-items:start;max-width:1700px;margin:0 auto}
.post-body{padding:1.5rem 2.5rem 6rem 2rem;min-width:0}
.post-body section{margin-bottom:4.5rem;scroll-margin-top:76px}
.post-body h2{font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:.875rem}
.post-body h3{font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text2);margin:1.75rem 0 .625rem}
.post-body p{font-size:.925rem;color:var(--muted2);margin-bottom:.875rem;line-height:1.75}
.post-body ul{list-style:none;margin-bottom:.875rem}
.post-body ul li{font-size:.925rem;color:var(--muted2);padding:.3rem 0 .3rem 1.4rem;position:relative;line-height:1.65}
.post-body ul li::before{content:'→';position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--purple);font-weight:700}
.section-no{font-size:.68rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--purple);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono)}

/* ── Viz panel ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
.vp{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin:1.75rem 0}
.vp-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:.65rem 1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface)}
.vp-title{font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted2)}
.vp-hint{font-size:.67rem;color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.3rem}
.vp-hint::before{content:'⟳';color:var(--cyan)}
.vp-body{padding:1.25rem}

/* ── Generation comparison ──────────────────────────────── */
.gen-cmp{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:var(--border);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;margin:1.75rem 0}
.gen-col{background:var(--card);padding:1.25rem}
.gen-col h4{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:1rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono)}
.gen-col.ar h4{color:var(--muted2)}
.gen-col.mtp h4{color:var(--cyan)}
.tok-stream{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.3rem;min-height:72px}
.tok{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:.18rem .55rem;border-radius:4px;font-family:var(--ff-mono);font-size:.76rem;font-weight:500;opacity:0;transform:translateY(5px);transition:opacity .25s,transform .25s}
.tok.show{opacity:1;transform:none}
.ar-col .tok{background:var(--card2);border:1px solid var(--border-hi);color:var(--text2)}
.mtp-col .b1.tok{background:var(--purple-dim);border:1px solid rgba(139,92,246,.3);color:var(--purple-l)}
.mtp-col .b2.tok{background:var(--cyan-dim);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,.3);color:var(--cyan)}
.mtp-col .b3.tok{background:var(--green-dim);border:1px solid rgba(16,185,129,.3);color:var(--green)}
.gen-stat-row{display:flex;gap:1.25rem;margin-top:1rem;padding-top:.875rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.gen-stat{font-size:.72rem;color:var(--muted)}
.gen-stat strong{display:block;font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.05rem}
.ar .gen-stat strong{color:var(--muted2)}
.mtp .gen-stat strong{color:var(--cyan)}

/* ── Accept / Reject ────────────────────────────────────── */
.ar-demo{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1rem;margin:1.5rem 0}
.ar-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}
.ar-label{font-size:.67rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);width:72px;flex-shrink:0;font-family:var(--ff-mono)}
.ar-tok{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.3rem;padding:.28rem .7rem;border-radius:6px;font-family:var(--ff-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:500;transition:all .4s}
.ar-tok.pending{background:var(--card2);border:1px solid var(--border-hi);color:var(--muted2)}
.ar-tok.accepted{background:var(--green-dim);border:1px solid rgba(16,185,129,.4);color:var(--green)}
.ar-tok.rejected{background:rgba(239,68,68,.09);border:1px solid rgba(239,68,68,.3);color:var(--red)}
.ar-tok .badge{font-size:.6rem;font-weight:700}

/* ── Attention grid ─────────────────────────────────────── */
.attn-wrap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.5rem;margin:1.5rem 0}
.attn-col h4{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.75rem;text-align:center;font-family:var(--ff-mono)}
.attn-col.causal-col h4{color:var(--muted2)}
.attn-col.bidir-col h4{color:var(--cyan)}
.attn-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(8,1fr);gap:2px}
.acell{aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:2px;transition:background .4s}
.acell.on-c{background:rgba(139,92,246,.75)}
.acell.off{background:rgba(255,255,255,.04)}
.acell.on-b{background:rgba(6,182,212,.75)}

/* ── Viz targets (clickable SVG regions) ────────────────── */
.vt{cursor:pointer;outline:none}
.vt:focus rect,.vt:hover rect{opacity:.85}
.vt.active rect:not(.vt-bg){stroke:var(--amber)!important;stroke-width:2!important}
.vt-glow{filter:drop-shadow(0 0 8px rgba(245,158,11,.5))}

/* ── Centroid viz ───────────────────────────────────────── */
.centroid-stage{position:relative}
.centroid-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;font-size:.75rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--cyan);background:var(--cyan-dim);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,.3);border-radius:6px;padding:.35rem .85rem;cursor:pointer;transition:all .2s;margin-top:.875rem}
.centroid-btn:hover{background:rgba(6,182,212,.2)}

/* ── PLE diagram ────────────────────────────────────────── */
.ple-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden}
.ple-table th,.ple-table td{font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);padding:.5rem .75rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.ple-table th{background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase}
.ple-table td:first-child{color:var(--muted2);width:80px}
.ple-table td:nth-child(2){color:var(--text2)}
.ple-table td:last-child{color:var(--purple-l)}
.ple-table tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}
.ple-table tr:hover td{background:rgba(255,255,255,.02)}

/* ── Code sidebar ───────────────────────────────────────── */
.code-sidebar{position:sticky;top:56px;height:calc(100vh - 56px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;border-left:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--code-bg)}
.cs-head{padding:.75rem 1.1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);flex-shrink:0}
.cs-file{font-size:.67rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.2rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem}
.cs-file::before{content:'';width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--purple);flex-shrink:0;display:inline-block}
.cs-section-title{font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text2)}
.cs-tabs{display:flex;overflow-x:auto;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);flex-shrink:0;scrollbar-width:none}
.cs-tabs::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
.cs-tab{font-size:.68rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);padding:.55rem .9rem;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;transition:all .15s;flex-shrink:0;background:none;border-top:none;border-left:none;border-right:none}
.cs-tab:hover{color:var(--text2);background:rgba(255,255,255,.025)}
.cs-tab.active{color:var(--purple-l);border-bottom-color:var(--purple);background:var(--purple-dim)}
.cs-body{flex:1;overflow-y:auto;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:thin;scrollbar-color:var(--border-hi) transparent}
.cs-panel{display:none}
.cs-panel.active{display:block}
.cs-pre{font-family:var(--ff-mono);font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.75;padding:.875rem 0;color:#abb2bf;white-space:pre}
.cs-line{display:block;padding:0 1.25rem}
.cs-line.hl-p{background:rgba(139,92,246,.12);border-left:2px solid var(--purple);margin:0 0;padding:0 1.1rem}
.cs-line.hl-c{background:rgba(6,182,212,.1);border-left:2px solid var(--cyan);margin:0 0;padding:0 1.1rem}
.cs-line.hl-g{background:rgba(16,185,129,.1);border-left:2px solid var(--green);margin:0 0;padding:0 1.1rem}
/* Syntax */
.kw{color:#c678dd}.fn{color:#61afef}.cls{color:#e5c07b}.str{color:#98c379}.cmt{color:#5c6370;font-style:italic}.num{color:#d19a66}.op{color:#abb2bf}.attr{color:#e06c75}

/* ── Responsive ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
@media(max-width:1100px){.post-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.code-sidebar{position:static;height:auto;border-left:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:2rem}.cs-body{max-height:480px}}
@media(max-width:680px){.post-hero{padding:5rem 1.25rem 2.5rem}.post-body{padding:1.25rem 1.25rem 4rem}.gen-cmp{grid-template-columns:1fr}.attn-wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ HERO -->
<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">Gemma 4</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Multi-Token Prediction</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Speculative Decoding</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>How Gemma 4's Multi-Token<br>Prediction Works</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Gemma 4 ships a compact <em>assistant model</em> that drafts multiple tokens per step — then the large backbone verifies them in a single parallel pass. This post tears apart the implementation: KV sharing, centroid-based vocabulary prediction, and bidirectional attention, with animated, code-annotated diagrams.
  </p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
    <span>May 24, 2026</span>
    <span>~15 min read</span>
    <span>Source: <code>transformers/models/gemma4_assistant</code></span>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ GRID -->
<div class="post-grid">

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════ ARTICLE ══════════════════ -->
<article class="post-body">

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §1 The Problem -->
<section id="s-intro" data-code="intro">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Problem</div>
<h2>Why standard generation is slow</h2>
<p>
  Large language models generate text <strong>one token at a time</strong>. Every new token requires a full forward pass through all N layers. On a 2B-parameter model that is fast; on a 27B model it becomes the throughput bottleneck. Because each token depends on the previous one, generation is inherently serial.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Multi-Token Prediction (MTP)</strong> — also called speculative decoding — breaks this constraint by running a lightweight <em>draft model</em> in parallel with the main model. The draft model proposes several tokens at once; the backbone verifies them all in a single pass. Accepted tokens are kept; rejected ones are discarded and the backbone corrects from that point. Net throughput gain: typically 2–4×.
</p>

<div class="gen-cmp">
  <div class="gen-col ar">
    <h4>Autoregressive (standard)</h4>
    <div class="tok-stream ar-col" id="ar-stream">
      <span class="tok" data-delay="0">The</span>
      <span class="tok" data-delay="600">capital</span>
      <span class="tok" data-delay="1200">of</span>
      <span class="tok" data-delay="1800">France</span>
      <span class="tok" data-delay="2400">is</span>
      <span class="tok" data-delay="3000">Paris</span>
      <span class="tok" data-delay="3600">.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gen-stat-row ar">
      <div class="gen-stat"><strong>1×</strong>baseline speed</div>
      <div class="gen-stat"><strong>7</strong>forward passes</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="gen-col mtp">
    <h4>Multi-Token Prediction</h4>
    <div class="tok-stream mtp-col" id="mtp-stream">
      <span class="tok b1" data-delay="0">The</span>
      <span class="tok b1" data-delay="80">capital</span>
      <span class="tok b1" data-delay="160">of</span>
      <span class="tok b2" data-delay="700">France</span>
      <span class="tok b2" data-delay="780">is</span>
      <span class="tok b2" data-delay="860">Paris</span>
      <span class="tok b3" data-delay="1400">.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gen-stat-row mtp">
      <div class="gen-stat"><strong>~3×</strong>typical speedup</div>
      <div class="gen-stat"><strong>2–3</strong>backbone passes</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-insight">
  <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
  <span>The draft model must be <em>extremely fast</em> — otherwise the overhead of drafting cancels the parallel-verification win. Gemma 4's assistant achieves this by reusing the backbone's KV cache and operating at a much smaller hidden dimension.</span>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §2 Architecture -->
<section id="s-arch" data-code="architecture">
<div class="section-no">02 — Architecture</div>
<h2>The two-model system</h2>
<p>
  The system consists of <code>Gemma4ForCausalLM</code> (the backbone) and <code>Gemma4AssistantForCausalLM</code> (the draft model). The backbone runs a standard forward pass and exposes its <strong>last-layer key-value states</strong> via <code>shared_kv_states</code>. The assistant reads these states to draft tokens without recomputing attention from scratch.
</p>
<p>Click any component below to see its source code in the sidebar.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">architecture-overview.svg</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">Click components to view code</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body" style="padding:.875rem">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 660 490" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">
      <!-- Main backbone box -->
      <rect x="8" y="8" width="644" height="170" rx="8" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.06)" stroke="rgba(139,92,246,.4)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="18" y="28" font-size="9" fill="#8b5cf6" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1" text-anchor="start">MAIN BACKBONE</text>
      <text x="18" y="42" font-size="11" fill="#e2e8f0" font-weight="600">Gemma4ForCausalLM</text>
      <text x="492" y="42" font-size="9" fill="#64748b">d_model = 1536</text>

      <!-- Embed sub-box -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-embed" data-target="architecture:embed" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="22" y="56" width="195" height="38" rx="5" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.1)" stroke="rgba(139,92,246,.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="119" y="71" font-size="9" fill="#a78bfa" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">ScaledWordEmbedding</text>
        <text x="119" y="84" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">+ Per-Layer Embeddings (PLE)</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Transformer layers -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-layers" data-target="architecture:layers" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="228" y="56" width="240" height="38" rx="5" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.08)" stroke="rgba(139,92,246,.25)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="348" y="71" font-size="9" fill="#a78bfa" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Transformer Layers</text>
        <text x="348" y="84" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">full_attn + sliding_window</text>
      </g>

      <!-- LM Head -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-lmhead" data-target="architecture:lmhead" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="479" y="56" width="170" height="38" rx="5" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.08)" stroke="rgba(139,92,246,.25)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="564" y="71" font-size="9" fill="#a78bfa" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">LM Head</text>
        <text x="564" y="84" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Linear(1536→vocab_size)</text>
      </g>

      <!-- KV cache box -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-kvcache" data-target="kv-sharing:cache" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="22" y="112" width="607" height="38" rx="5" fill="rgba(16,185,129,.07)" stroke="rgba(16,185,129,.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="325" y="127" font-size="9" fill="#10b981" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">shared_kv_states</text>
        <text x="325" y="140" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">dict["full_attention" | "sliding_attention"] → (key, value) tensors  ← exposed to assistant</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Connector zone arrows -->
      <line x1="200" y1="186" x2="200" y2="268" stroke="rgba(16,185,129,.4)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,3"/>
      <line x1="460" y1="186" x2="460" y2="268" stroke="rgba(16,185,129,.4)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,3"/>
      <polygon points="196,264 200,272 204,264" fill="rgba(16,185,129,.6)"/>
      <polygon points="456,264 460,272 464,264" fill="rgba(16,185,129,.6)"/>
      <!-- Flowing dots on connector -->
      <circle class="flow-dot fd1" cx="200" cy="200" r="3" fill="#10b981" opacity=".9"/>
      <circle class="flow-dot fd2" cx="460" cy="210" r="3" fill="#10b981" opacity=".9"/>
      <text x="290" y="232" font-size="8" fill="#10b981" text-anchor="middle" font-style="italic">shared_kv_states passed to assistant</text>

      <!-- Assistant box -->
      <rect x="8" y="272" width="644" height="202" rx="8" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.05)" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.35)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="18" y="292" font-size="9" fill="#06b6d4" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1">DRAFT MODEL</text>
      <text x="18" y="306" font-size="11" fill="#e2e8f0" font-weight="600">Gemma4AssistantForCausalLM</text>
      <text x="480" y="306" font-size="9" fill="#64748b">d_model = 768</text>

      <!-- pre_projection -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-preprojection" data-target="projections:pre" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="22" y="316" width="165" height="44" rx="5" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.1)" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="104" y="333" font-size="9" fill="#06b6d4" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">pre_projection</text>
        <text x="104" y="347" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Linear(2×1536 → 768)</text>
        <text x="104" y="358" font-size="7.5" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">concat backbone hid</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Arrow pre → transformer -->
      <line x1="187" y1="338" x2="205" y2="338" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.4)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      <polygon points="202,334.5 208,338 202,341.5" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.6)"/>

      <!-- Transformer -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-asst-layers" data-target="kv-sharing:forward" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="210" y="316" width="235" height="44" rx="5" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.08)" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.25)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="327" y="333" font-size="9" fill="#06b6d4" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Transformer Layers</text>
        <text x="327" y="347" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">uses shared_kv_states</text>
        <text x="327" y="358" font-size="7.5" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">bidirectional attention</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Arrow transformer → post -->
      <line x1="445" y1="338" x2="462" y2="338" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.4)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      <polygon points="459,334.5 465,338 459,341.5" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.6)"/>

      <!-- post_projection -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-postprojection" data-target="projections:post" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="466" y="316" width="175" height="44" rx="5" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.1)" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="553" y="333" font-size="9" fill="#06b6d4" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">post_projection</text>
        <text x="553" y="347" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Linear(768 → 1536)</text>
        <text x="553" y="358" font-size="7.5" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">back to backbone dim</text>
      </g>

      <!-- MaskedEmbedder -->
      <g class="vt" id="vt-masked" data-target="centroid:embedder" tabindex="0" role="button">
        <rect x="22" y="378" width="220" height="44" rx="5" fill="rgba(245,158,11,.07)" stroke="rgba(245,158,11,.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="132" y="395" font-size="9" fill="#f59e0b" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">MaskedEmbedder</text>
        <text x="132" y="409" font-size="8" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">centroid-based vocab pred</text>
        <text x="132" y="420" font-size="7.5" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">if use_ordered_embeddings</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Draft output -->
      <text x="325" y="456" font-size="9" fill="#06b6d4" text-anchor="middle" font-style="italic">draft logits → speculative decoding verification by backbone</text>
      <line x1="325" y1="474" x2="325" y2="485" stroke="rgba(6,182,212,.4)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <polygon points="321,481 325,488 329,481" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.6)"/>
    </svg>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-tip">
  <span class="callout-icon">⚡</span>
  <span>The assistant's transformer is much <em>smaller</em> than the backbone (fewer layers, smaller hidden dim). It is fast enough that drafting 3–4 tokens costs less than one backbone forward pass.</span>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §3 KV Sharing -->
<section id="s-kv" data-code="kv-sharing">
<div class="section-no">03 — KV Sharing</div>
<h2>Reusing the backbone's attention states</h2>
<p>
  The key insight: the assistant does not need its own KV cache. Instead, it <strong>borrows the backbone's last-layer key-value tensors</strong>. The backbone's <code>Gemma4TextModel.forward()</code> returns a <code>shared_kv_states</code> dict whenever <code>return_shared_kv_states=True</code>. The assistant receives this dict and passes it through all its layers.
</p>
<p>
  Since the assistant shares KV from <em>all</em> layers (the config forces <code>num_kv_shared_layers = num_hidden_layers</code>), it never computes its own key/value projections — saving roughly half the attention FLOPS.
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">kv-sharing-flow.svg</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">Animated data flow</span>
